title: The Supreme Court announces the formation of the Royal Tribunal
new-page: true

## Finished, but could be polished a lot more

- @option_intro_1: Another day comes to an end...

@option_intro_1
subtitle: ...and another one begins anew.
new-page: true

= An early morning

You wake up quite early in the morning as the sun is yet to be visible above the horizon.

You feel pleasantly surprised. It has been quite a while since you've managed to wake up this early, after all.

However, that pleasant feeling does not last very long. As you prepare for the day, your mind wanders about...

- @the_news: The possibility of a public trial.

@the_news

...the possibility that the Princess herself would face a public trial. The uncomfortable hunch from yesterday's discussion still persists, and what you — and perhaps everyone else — thought was unthinkable is now creeping ever closer to become a certain reality.

At this point, you don't know if the fact that there is no precedent to this issue is comforting, or actually terrifying instead. This is a completely new territory that no one has ever breached before in history, and whatever happens next, no matter how insignificant it is, will be decisive.

- @next_up: And then...

@next_up

Before you realize it, the sun is already well above the horizon, and the sky has already turned a rather bright blue.

You quickly finish up your preparation before heading towards the door. Everything is nicely put into the bag, and you are now ready to go.

- @head_out: It's time to head out.

@head_out
new-page: true

- @newspaper_1: The morning newspaper has arrived!

@newspaper_1
new-page: true

The morning newspaper arrives in front of the door right as you are about to head out. Hesitantly, you pick it up to read what the headline said.

- @headline: And the headline reads...

@headline

= The Supreme Court announces the formation of the Royal Tribunal!

*And the scandal surrounding the Princess of Nocturnia is officially heading to a public trial!*

- @what: ...

@what

Unconsciously, your grip on the newspaper tightens as dread begins to fill your mind. Things have been moving way too fast, way too quickly for you to properly keep up.

A nauseating feeling begins to rise up your throat. 

- @a_way_out: Is there even a way out of this?

@a_way_out

*"Is there even a way out of this?"* you ponder inwardly as you fold the newspaper into your bag.

Frankly, you don't even know what to feel about the announcement. On one hand, it saves Princess Darlyne from the immediate worst-case scenario, which would have undoubtedly been severe. On the other, however, the direction of this tribunal is going to be unpredictable.

It's not that far-fetched to imagine that the tribunal's verdict has been pre-determined from the start, rendering it no different to a <span class="tooltip-text" title="A public trial in which the guilt or innocence of the defendant has already been determined.">show trial</span>. Even worse, it might as well be <span class="tooltip-text" title="A court that ignores established standards of law or justice and may ignore due process to arrive at a predetermined conclusion.">A kangaroo court</span> of sorts. A shame to the entire nation.

*No*, you shake your head quickly, *this train of thoughts has to stop.*

You hope that it is simply your mind playing up to the occasion, imagining every possible outcome — even the worst ones. You shake your head once more.

With the sun already shining brightly in the sky, you pick up your bag as you quickly run towards the carriage heading to the Royal Palace.

- @next_page

@next_page
